@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Configuration
  "Loads the per-machine ~/.mason and the nearest project .mason, merges them, and resolves servers, sites, and the share store with derived defaults (config v2; see CONFIG.md)."

  Provides:
    - config.Config @source("symbol:Config")
    - config.Server @source("symbol:Server")
    - config.Site @source("symbol:Site")
    - config.Share @source("symbol:Share")
    - config.LoadOptions @source("symbol:LoadOptions")
    - config.Load @source("symbol:Load")
    - config.ParseServer @source("symbol:ParseServer")
    - config.Config.Site @source("symbol:Site")
    - config.Config.RequireShare @source("symbol:RequireShare")
    - config.V1FormatError @source("symbol:V1FormatError")
    - config.NewSite @source("symbol:NewSite")
    - config.NewShare @source("symbol:NewShare")

  Invariants:
    - Load MUST merge ~/.mason with the nearest project .mason; a project file MUST NOT hide the user file
    - Project discovery MUST walk upward from the start dir and MUST NOT treat the user file itself (~/.mason) as a project file
    - A project file MUST NOT define share; the share store MUST come only from the user file, so share commands can never target a site's web root
    - The user file MUST NOT define site, sites, or build
    - A file using the v1 shape (targets/default keys) MUST fail with V1FormatError pointing at CONFIG.md
    - Unknown keys MUST be rejected with the file, line, and the closest valid key when one is near
    - A site's identity (Name default, snippet, cache) MUST derive from its URL host; two sites in one project MUST NOT share a host
    - Site and share URLs MUST reduce to scheme://host; a URL with a path MUST be rejected; a bare host MUST default to https
    - Site and share paths MUST default to /var/www/<url host>
    - Server resolution MUST prefer site server, then project server, then user server; the SSH user MUST default to "mason"
    - The first entry under sites MUST be the default site
    - NewSite and NewShare MUST apply exactly the same normalization and defaults as Load
    - Missing pieces (no server, no share, no sites) MUST surface as actionable errors only when a command asks for them, never at Load

  OutOfScope:
    - Writing or editing config files (setup and init own that)
    - SSH option rendering and connection behavior (internal/remote)
    - Existence checks for build directories (deploy owns that)

  Scenario (happy-path): Two-line project file
    Given ~/.mason with server and share, and a project .mason with site and build
    When Load runs from a subdirectory of the project
    Then the site resolves with path /var/www/<host>, user mason, and the user file's server

  Scenario (happy-path): Environments
    Given a project with sites staging and live
    When Site("") and Site("live") are called
    Then staging is the default and live resolves by name or by host

  Scenario (negative): Share in a project file
    Given a project .mason with a share key
    When Load runs
    Then it fails explaining that share belongs in ~/.mason

  Scenario (negative): v1 file
    Given a .mason with default and targets keys
    When Load runs
    Then it returns V1FormatError naming the file and CONFIG.md

  Scenario (negative): No server anywhere
    Given a project site and no server in either file
    When Site is called
    Then it fails suggesting mason setup <host>

  Scenario (edge): Run from the home directory
    Given cwd is $HOME, where ~/.mason exists
    When Load runs
    Then ~/.mason is loaded as the user file and no project is found
